1.0.0: the developing release

Two axes complete the camera / film / develop / age model.

Development: --develop {normal, push+1, push+2, pull-1, cross} on the
CLI and a Developing selector on the web. Push raises display-referred
contrast and coarsens grain, pull relaxes both, cross-processing
applies crossed per-channel curves (green-yellow highlights, cool
crushed shadows, high contrast and saturation). All are chemistry, so
they run after the color stage and compose with any film LUT - and all
are refused, with a note, for instant cameras, whose development is
sealed inside the film unit; the web disables the selector for them.

Film catalog: the staged library grows from eleven stocks to the
historically important families - Kodachrome 25/64/200 (K-14),
Ektachrome and Elite (E-6), the Fuji slide line, three generations of
Portra including the NC/VC/UC era, the Superia ladder, Kodak and
Ilford and Agfa/Rollei black-and-white, the Polaroid integral and
pack-film chemistries, and measured cross-processed stocks - grouped
in the film selector with process labels, and documented family by
family in the help panel.

One point zero: nine days from an unanchored tone curve to a
camera/film/develop/age model, thirteen cameras spanning 1907-2005,
byte-identical native and WebAssembly rendering, and a one-command
release pipeline.
